{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:437312d74e8c998d","name":"Enforcer (CL 5)","source":{"id":"source:reference-437312d74e8c998d","title":"Enforcer (CL 5)","revision":25236,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:15:39Z","sha256":"90b411f7a6736d2fd2bae65c7dc5d0e16eec741e59444fef89bb40cceb896beb","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25236","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Enforcer%20%28CL%205%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-437312d74e8c998d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Enforcers exist somewhere between government authority figures (such as soldiers or law officers) and the common thugs used by crime lords and pirates. Enforcers have a legal right to be armed, but they lack the kind of legitimacy of major military and paramilitary organizations. Enforcers might work for major corporations (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Corporate Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Corporate_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bbbb4f654660345b"},"), independent merchants, wide-scale criminal organizations with internal rules and regulations (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Smugglers' Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Smugglers%27_Alliance?action=edit&redlink=1"},"), or fringe quasi-governments like shadowports (such as security forces on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Errant Venture"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Errant_Venture","referenceId":"reference:7d17b0c46c7603c7"},"). Others have official power but lack the training and jurisdiction of law officers, such as prison guards or a Moff's private security force.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Enforcers have a bad reputation across the galaxy. Lacking the skills needed to carefully track down potential troublemakers or to sift through evidence to determine guilt, Enforcers might react to trouble with quick and overwhelming violence. This prevents any wrongdoer from getting away- and dead men don't complain about their innocence. Enforcers don't usually distinguish between the guilty and the innocent; they let the blaster bolts sort out who lives and who dies.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Enforcer Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 5\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 21 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 19), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 21, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 16; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Combat Reflexes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combat_Reflexes","referenceId":"reference:eefac0ff23eeb160"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children"